<h2 class="doc_title">Nadeem vs State Of U.P. And 4 Others on 23 July, 2024</h2>
<h2 class="doc_title">Nadeem vs State Of U.P. And 4 Others on 23 July, 2024</h2>

<h3 class="doc_author">Author: <a href="/search/?formInput=authorid:m-k-gupta">Manoj Kumar Gupta</a></h3>

<h3 class="doc_bench">Bench: <a href="/search/?formInput=benchid:m-k-gupta">Manoj Kumar Gupta</a></h3>

<pre id="pre_1">




HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT ALLAHABAD
 
 


?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:AHC:116653-DB
 
Court No. - 21
 

 
Case :- WRIT - C No. - 15996 of 2024
 
Petitioner :- Nadeem
 
Respondent :- State Of U.P. And 4 Others
 
Counsel for Petitioner :- Ram Brij Napit
 
Counsel for Respondent :- Alok Mishra,C.S.C.
 

 
Hon&#x27;ble Manoj Kumar Gupta,J.
 
</pre><p data-structure="Precedent" id="p_1">Hon&#x27;ble Manish Kumar Nigam,J.
</p> 
<p data-structure="Issue" id="p_2">1. Counter affidavit filed on behalf of respondent nos. 4 and 5, is taken on record.
</p> 
<p data-structure="Issue" id="p_3">2. Prayer made in the instant petition is for quashing the recovery citation dated 22.2.2024, issued by respondent no. 3, for recovery of electricity dues from the petitioner in a case of theft of electricity.
</p> 
<p data-structure="Issue" id="p_4">3. Indisputably, there is an order of final assessment against the petitioner under <a href="/doc/124046987/" id="a_1">Section 126</a> of the Electricity Act, 2003, whereunder he has to pay Rs. 99,842/-. Since the said amount has not been paid by the petitioner, therefore, the impugned recovery certificate has been issued.
</p> 
<p data-structure="PetArg" id="p_5">4. It appears from the counter affidavit that the petitioner has challenged the assessment order before Permanent Lok Adalat, Aligarh in Case No. 51 of 2023 and the said proceedings are pending. The aforesaid fact has not been disclosed by the petitioner in the writ petition. 
</p> 
<p data-structure="PetArg" id="p_6">5. Learned counsel for the petitioner after making brief submissions, submits that the petitioner is ready to pay the entire outstanding amount in installments and that the electricity connection to the petitioners premises be directed to be restored. 
</p> 
<p data-structure="RespArg" id="p_7">6. Sri Alok Mishra, learned counsel for the respondent-Electricity Department, has no objection in permitting the petitioner to deposit the amount in installments. 
</p> 
<p data-structure="RespArg" id="p_8">7. In respect of restoration of electricity supply, he submits that permanent disconnection was affected on 29.2.2024 and therefore the electricity supply can be restored only upon a proper application being filed by the petitioner as per the procedure prescribed under U.P. Electricity Supply Code, 2005. 
</p> 
<p data-structure="CDiscource" id="p_9">8. Having regard to the submissions made and with consent of learned counsel for the parties, we dispose of the instant petition as follows: -
</p> 
<blockquote id="blockquote_1">(a) The petitioner will deposit the sum due under the recovery certificate in four equal monthly installments. 
</blockquote> 
<blockquote id="blockquote_2">(b) The first installment will become due and payable on 15.8.2024, the next one on 15.9.2024 and so on, so that the last installment would become payable on 15.11.2024. 
</blockquote> 
<blockquote id="blockquote_3">(c) It shall be open for the petitioner to apply for restoration of electricity connection as per the procedure prescribed under the U.P. Electricity Supply Code, 2005. 
</blockquote> 
<blockquote id="blockquote_4">(d) In case any such application is made, it shall be considered in accordance with law, as soon as the second installment is paid by the petitioner.
</blockquote> 

 
<p data-structure="Precedent" id="p_10">(Manish Kumar Nigam, J.)  (Manoj Kumar Gupta, J.)
 
Order Date :- 23.7.2024
 
Jaideep/-
</p> 



 




 

 
 
    
      
  
 
